iMac 5K stitch: report the slave tile's connector as disconnected

With amdgpu.tiled_stitch=1 the slave tile is already marked non-desktop, but
its connector still reads "connected", so compositors list it (Hyprland shows a
disabled DP-1 and assigns it a crtc) and Omarchy's display panel offers a
"DP-1" row whose click runs `hyprctl keyword monitor DP-1,preferred,...` --
enabling the tile as a second output underneath the stitched one. The slave is
part of the one panel; report it disconnected and every consumer sees exactly
one display. dc_link/sink state is untouched, so the peer stream is unaffected.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -8691,6 +8691,20 @@
 	else if (aconnector->base.force == DRM_FORCE_OFF)
 		return connector_status_disconnected;
 
+	/*
+	 * Tiled stitch: the slave tile is part of the one stitched panel, not a
+	 * display of its own -- the root connector presents all 5120 columns
+	 * and this tile is driven as the root crtc's peer stream. Report it
+	 * disconnected so no compositor claims a crtc for it and no settings
+	 * panel offers to switch it on as a second output (non_desktop alone
+	 * still leaves it listed). The dc_link and its sink stay intact: the
+	 * peer stream, the boot re-probe and link recovery use those, not this
+	 * status. Without tiled_stitch the tile is reported as usual, for
+	 * compositors that stitch the pair themselves.
+	 */
+	if (amdgpu_dm_link_is_tiled_stitch_slave(aconnector->dc_link))
+		return connector_status_disconnected;
+
 	/* Poll analog connectors and only when either
 	 * disconnected or connected to an analog display.
 	 */
